// @skip-os: win32
// asserts on a diagnostic that quotes string.h's strlen spelling; the MSVC CRT
// declares it differently, so the compile fails for a different reason.

// @error: Milo writes through a *u32 (4-byte pointee)
// An out-param's pointee width IS the contract — it is how many bytes the callee
// writes into the caller's frame. Nothing else in the pipeline can see this: the ABI
// passes one word whatever the pointee, so a wrong pointee links, runs, and scribbles.
@cSig("string.h", "size_t strlen(const char *)")
extern fn strlen(s: *u32): u64

fn main() {
    print(1)
}
